.TH SAPHIRA 7 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "Overview"
.SH NAME
saphira \- Saphira Linux native packaging concepts and tooling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man recipe
.RS
The recipe file format,
.BR recipe (5),
is the canonical contract.
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Saphira Linux builds itself from native package recipes (see
.BR recipe (5)).
A recipe plus its
.I files/
tree compiles, in a disposable rootless container, into one or more
immutable signed APKs published to a generation repository.
.PP
Generations are append-only archives that become the live view:
.I hatchling
holds full history (including retired r0 artifacts),
.I hatched
is the current view. A published NVR (name-version-release) is
immutable: the published copy always wins, rebuilds retire as evidence,
and package revisions start at r1 (r0 is forbidden outside hatchling
history).
.PP
Builds resolve dependencies repository-first and install only into
their own merged root; nothing is ever copied from the controller
host into a build. Publication is gated (file ownership, Unix
identities, reservations) and indexed; installation on targets is
exact-NVR and service identities are created at install time by the
packaged declarations, never by hand.
.PP
Essential runtime lives in
.IR /bin ,
.IR /sbin ,
.IR /lib ;
general material lives under
.IR /usr .
A binary in
.I /bin
or
.I /sbin
must not require anything under
.IR /usr/lib ;
a binary in
.I /usr/bin
may use both
.I /lib
and
.IR /usr/lib .
Development material (headers, pkg-config/CMake metadata) lives under
.IR /usr .
.SH OPTIONS
This page takes no options; it is a concept overview.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /recipes
Recipe tree (one directory per package, each with
.IR recipe.sh ).
.TP
.I /build
Scratch build workspaces (one per top-level build; failures retained
as diagnostic evidence).
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/
Generation repositories per architecture, with indexes and the
.I repository.db
metadata database.
.TP
.I /out/stage4/incoming/
Unsigned
.I *-ready
staging transactions awaiting publication.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Not applicable (documentation only).
.SH EXAMPLES
Read the contract first, then the tool for the job at hand:
.PP
.RS
man 5 recipe
.br
man 1 buildpkg
.br
man 8 sign-apk-repo
.RE
